      "message": "Please fix this WARNING reported by autoreview issue finding: Since `vboot_is_padding_valid` appears to validate padding alignment (e.g., returning `EC_ERROR_INVAL` for unaligned indices), it likely casts this pointer internally to a larger type (like `uint32_t*` or `uint64_t*`). \n\nBecause local `uint8_t` arrays aren\u0027t guaranteed to be word-aligned on the stack, this could potentially cause an unaligned access fault on some architectures. \n\nConsider aligning it explicitly (e.g. `uint8_t data[64] __aligned(4);`) or using `uint32_t data[64 / sizeof(uint32_t)];` and casting it.",
